From 37be830c3d35f88ba60540f970fe32b719de69a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nekreshen@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:38:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] frame generation for a title without guest markers, on Metal

What FIFA 19's cut-scenes (30 FPS, the game's own minimum frame time)
needed to get MetalFX frame interpolation to 60:

- guest_marker_rules: a title names the pixel shaders where its tone
  map and UI begin; the markers are given at those draws (tone map after
  the temporal pass's check, so the pass runs at the same draw).
- temporal_aa_anchor_ps takes several shaders (one per kind of scene),
  and the camera is the scene's last matching draw's (the first could
  still hold the last frame's matrix: a cut seen a frame late).
- Camera cuts seen in the cameras: the centre ray turning 10 degrees or
  jumping 4 of its lengths (cuts move it 20-600; tracking shots 0.7 a
  frame); temporal_aa_debug 11 logs the check.
- UIDrawer/ImGuiDialog::HasContent: the achievement notifier, always
  registered, counts as UI only while it shows a toast, so generated
  frames are not held back under a UI that draws nothing.
- The Metal presenter asks for a generated frame only while the game's
  frames are far enough apart for it to be shown (4-5 ms of GPU each).

FIFA 19: the walk-out at 60 on screen (300 generated frames presented
in 10 s, 11 cuts reset in a walk-out), matches at 60 generate nothing.
